@      *$SET TRACE ASMLIST COPYLIST PARAS REF
       IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
       PROGRAM-ID.   MPTZ021.
       AUTHOR.       PENNY GENOVESE.
       DATE-WRITTEN. JANUARY 30, 1992
      *******************************************************************
      *SYSTEM NAME:   EDITORIAL SYSTEMS
      *APPL NAME:     OEM PARTS UPDATE
      *PROGRAM NAME:  MPTZ021 - TRANSACTION SPLIT PROGRAM
      *LANGUAGE:      COBOL II / Oracle
      *
      *DESCRIPTION:
      * FUNCTION:  THIS PROGRAM READS THE REFORMATTED TRANSACTION FILE
      *            AND WRITES THE FIVE TRANSACTION TYPES INTO SEPARATE
      *            DATASETS FOR INPUT TO THE UPDATE PROGRAMS.
      *
      *  INPUT:    CONTROL INFORMATION (PROGRAM PARM FILE)
      *            REFORMATTED TRANSACTION FILE
      *            Oracle OEM TABLE
      *            Oracle PARTS TABLE
      *
      *  OUTPUT:   ASSEMBLY TRANSACTION FILE
      *            COMPONENT TRANSACTION FILE
      *            SUPERSESSION TRANSACTION FILE
      *            DISCONTINUE TRANSACTION FILE
      *            PRICING TRANSACTION FILE
      *            CONTROL TOTAL / ERROR REPORTS
      *            Oracle REPORT TABLE
      *
      * SIGNIFICANT PROCESSING NARRATIVE:
      *            THIS PROGRAM CHECKS FOR VALID TRANSACTION TYPES**
      *            (A,C,D,N,P,R) AND FOR DUPLICATE PRICE TRANSACTIONS
      *            (BASED ON OLD PART NUMBER). IT ALSO CHECKS FOR
      *            LARGE PRICE VARIANCES BY COMPARING THE FIRST 20
      *            PRICE RECS AGAINST THE EXISTING Oracle PRICE. IF
      *            THERE IS A VARIANCE OF 90% OR MORE, AN ERROR REPORT
      *            IS WRITTEN INDICATING THAT THE PRICE FIELD POSITION
      *            MAY BE OFF ON THE OEM TAPE.
      *            **NOTE - "GENERATED ASSEMBLIES" WILL BE REMARKED
      *                     AND REWRITTEN AS ASSEMBLY RECORDS.
      *
      * CALLED PROGRAMS:
      *    CALL "dberrmsg" USING SQLCA ERROR-MESSAGE ERROR-LENGTH.
      *
      * CONTROL CARD:
      *  (SAME CONTROL CARD THAT'S USED IN THE UPDATE PROGRAMS)
      *
      *  OEM=XXX,REGN=XX,EFFDT=XX/XX/XXXX,REPLACE=X,RUNTYP-XXX,
      *       1        2           3              4         5
      *
      *  NAGSTYP=XXXXXXXX
      *              6
      *
      *       1 - NUMERIC; OEM NUMBER WHICH YOU ARE PROCESSING
      *
      *       2 - ALPHA; REGION OF THE OEM
      *
      *       3 - NUMERIC; PRICE EFFECTIVE DATE AS SPECIFIED BY THE
      *           OEM  (FORMAT MM/DD/YYYY; MUST BE GREATER THAN LAST RUN
      *           UNLESS THIS IS REPLACEMENT RUN- THEN MUST <= LAST RUN)
      *
      *       4 - ALPHA; REPLACEMENT INDICATOR (FOR PRICE UPDATE PGM);
      *           (N = NEW RUN, PRICES WILL BE UPDATED - CURRENT MOVED
      *           TO PREVIOUS THEN TRANSACTION PRICE MOVED TO CURRENT;
      *           Y = REPLACEMENT RUN, TRANSACTION PRICE MOVED DIRECTLY
      *           OVER CURRENT PRICE; USED FOR CORRECTING MISPRICING.)
      *
      *       5 - ALPHA; TYPE OF RUN (OEM = OEM, SUP = SUPPLIMENTAL)
      *           (USED BY REPORT PROGRAM MPTZ007)
      *
      *       6 - ALPHA; TYPE OF NAGS RUN (FOR NAGS RUN, EITHER "IMPORT"
      *           OR "DOMESTIC"; ANY OTHER RUNS, "N/A")
      *           (PRINTED IN HEADING - JUST TO DISTINGUISH BETWEEN THE
      *            IMPORT AND DOMESTIC RUN REPORTS)
      *
      * MODIFICATION LOG:
      * ----------------------------------------------------------------
      * 01/21/2019  BY:   PENNY GENOVESE
      *             DESC: Chg'd counters from 9(6) to 9(7) due to abend.
      * ----------------------------------------------------------------
      * 10/06/2014  BY:   PENNY GENOVESE
      *             DESC: Added Mod Note. Test new check_in & prod_move
      * ----------------------------------------------------------------
      * 05/17/2014  BY:   PENNY GENOVESE
      *             DESC: NO CODE CHANGES MADE. ADDED MOD NOTE SO THAT 
      *                   PROGRAM COULD BE RECOMPILED FOR ORACLE 11G /
      *                   IBM 770 MIGRATION.
      * ----------------------------------------------------------------
      * 07/23/2012  BY:   Patty Becotte
      *             DESC: Modified Z1100-REFMT-BALANCING to check if OEM
      *                   sends history and abend accordingly.
      *                   Added Z1120-GET-OEM-JOB-HIST-SUPER to query 
      *                   database for oem_job.hist_super_received_flag
      * ----------------------------------------------------------------
      * 07/13/2007  BY:   Gail Walder
      *             DESC: Modify Z1500-UPDATE-MEDIA-DETAIL for more 
      *                 descriptive message when media detail row does
      *                 not meet all criteria.
      * ----------------------------------------------------------------
      * 02/13/2006  BY:   Janet Wilson
      *             DESC: Correct Electronic Balancing Logic.
      *                   ---------   PROBLEM  -------------------------
      *                   At the start of this program values for
      *                   WS-LAST-PRICE-DATE and WS-LAST-PRICE-IND
      *                   are populated (p_part_suplrcntry_suplr_sel_01).
      *                   Then 'P' records are read and checked and the 
      *                   values for WS-LAST-PRICE-DATE and 
      *                   WS-LAST-PRICE-IND are OVERWRITTEN 
      *                   (pkg_part.p_part_sel_01). This didn't appear to 
      *                   be a problem, but in some, the "special" price 
      *                   transactions (mptr950.ksh) have a different
      *                   WS-LAST-PRICE-DATE than the part_supplier_country 
      *                   table, so the program abends.
      *                   SOLUTION:
      *                   Save values returned by 
      *                   p_part_suplrcntry_suplr_sel_01 and use those 
      *                   values in the Electronic Balancing Logic.
      * ----------------------------------------------------------------
      * 03/24/2004  BY:   LITA MIRANDA
      *             DESC: ADDED LOGIC TO:
      *                   1) CHECK FOR PART NUMBER OF "0" IN BOTH OLD
      *                      AND NEW PART NUM FIELDS
      *                      (AN OEM SENT US PARTS SUPERSEDING TO "0")
      *                   2) CHECK IF PART NUMBER CONTAINS VALID
      *                      ALPHANUMERIC CHARACTERS
      * ----------------------------------------------------------------
      * 12/30/2003  BY:   PENNY GENOVESE
      *             DESC: CHANGED BALANCING LOGIC TO:
      *                   1) USE NAGS_TYPE WHEN BALANCING SO THAT IT'S
      *                      COMPARING "LIKE" RUNS (E.G. CA FORD ALLPART
      *                      RUN TO CA FORD ALLPART RUN, RATHER THAN TO
      *                      AUTOCHG RUN.)
      *                   2) FOR NON US/CA RUNS (I.E. GLOBAL), PERFORMS
      *                      LESS-RESTRICTIVE BALANCING.
      *                   3) DON'T CAUSE AN EBS ABEND IF CURRENT INVALID
      *                      COUNT IS ZERO BUT PREVIOUS ONE WASN'T. (IT
      *                      JUST MEANS THEY'VE FIXED PRIOR ERRORS.)
      *                   4) UPDATE THE MEDIA DETAIL ROW, IF THE BALANCE
      *                      COMMENT IS "OKAY". (SAVES PROD CNTL TIME.)
      *                   5) ERROR MESSAGES ARE BRACKETED BY ASTERISKS.
      * ----------------------------------------------------------------
      * 07/12/2002  BY:   PENNY GENOVESE
      *             DESC: CORRECTED CODE SO THAT REFORMAT BALANCE REC IS
      *                   WRITTEN WHEN VARIANCE ERROR OCCURS.
      * ----------------------------------------------------------------
      * 11/29/2001  BY:   GAIL WALDER
      *             DESC: ADDED PRODUCTION CHANGES:
      *                   1. BY LITA MIRANDA - INCREASED SIZES OF
      *                      WS-ALLOWABLE-WHOLE-NUM AND WS-RESULT-WHOLE-NUM
      *                      TO PREVENT TRUNCATION OF CALCULATED RESULTS.
      *                   2. BY PENNY GENOVESE - MODIFIED TO WRITE REPORT
      *                      BALANCING ROW BEFORE PRICE VARIANCE VALIDATION
      *                      AND POSSIBLE ABEND.
      * ----------------------------------------------------------------
      * 05/08/2001  BY:   GAIL WALDER
      *             DESC: CORRECTED ELECTRONIC BALANCING DISPLAYS
      *                   TO THE LOG
      * ----------------------------------------------------------------
      * 04/25/01  BY:   LITA MIRANDA
      *           DESC: RACE II RETROFIT
      *                 CORRECTED CALCULATION TO CAUSE AN ABEND WHEN
      *                 WS-LAST-COUNT = 0 AND WS-THIS-COUNT > 0
      * ----------------------------------------------------------------
      * 02/09/01  BY: MARINA BOGOPOLSKY
      *          DESC:  ADDED Y1500-SQL-PROCEDURE-ERROR PARAGRAPH
      * ----------------------------------------------------------------
      * 12/17/20000 BY:    GAIL WALDER
      *             DESC:  CHANGED OVERLOADED BIND VARIABLE
      *                    WS-CURRENT-EFFECTIVE-DATE
      *                    TO WS-CURRENT-EFFECTIVE-DATE-IN
      *                    IN CALL TO P_ACQ_REFORMAT_BALANCE_SEL_01
      *                    BECAUSE PREVIOUS DATE FROM SELECT WAS INSERTED
      *                    INTO NEW REFORMAT BALANCE ROW.
      * ----------------------------------------------------------------
      * 11/14/2000  BY:    MARINA BOGOPOLSKY
      *             DESC:  RETROFITED ACCORDING TO KIM DINH'S CHANGES
      *                      11/02/2000
      *                    - TO DISPLAY CURRENT-EFFECTIVE-DATE AND
      *                    UPDATE-BALANCE-RUN-DATE (ACQ_REFORMAT_BALANCE
      *                    TABLE)
      *                    - CALLS TO P_ACQ_REFORMAT_BALANCE_SEL_01
      *                    - TO COMMIT ALL CHANGES TO REPORT TABLE
      *                    AFTER ALL CHECKINGS ARE SUCESSFUL
      * ----------------------------------------------------------------
      * 05/16/2000  BY:    JOHN NERIO
      *             DESC:  RACE II REVISIONS
      *                  1. CONVERTED FOR NEW DATABASE STRUCTURE
      *                  2. CONVERTED EMBEDDED SQL TO PKG/PROCEDURE CALLS
      * ----------------------------------------------------------------
      * 05/08/2000  BY:  KIM DINH
      *             DESC : ADD CURR-EFF-DT TO ALL QUERIES THAT ACCESS
      *                    IIST001 AND IIST002 TABLES.
      * ----------------------------------------------------------------
      * 01/11/2000  BY:  KIM DINH
      *             DESC:  ADDED LOGIC TO CAPTURE THE REC CNT FOR EACH TYPE
      *                    OF RECORD FROM THE SPLIT PROCESS AND BALANCE THESE
      *                    COUNTS AGAINST THE LAST RUN COUNTS TO DETERMINE
      *                    IF THE NUM OF RECS CHANGES BETWEEN TWO RUN IS
      *                    MET ALLOWABLE VARIANCE. ABEND JOB IF IT IS NOT
      * ----------------------------------------------------------------
      *
      * 10/18/98  BY:   Y2K TEAM
      *           DESC: ADDED CODE TO MAKE PROGRAM Y2K COMPLIANT.
      *                 ALL CODE MODIFIED MANUALLY AND BY SF2000
      *                 IS PREFIXED WITH 'BEGIN Y2K FIX' AND IS
      *                 TERMINATED BY 'END Y2K FIX'.
      * ----------------------------------------------------------------
      * 05/22/98  BY: GAIL WALDER
      *           DESC: REMOVED rEFERENCES IN DOCUMENTATION TO UK AND
      *                 SPECIAL cANADA oEM nUMBERS.  PREPARATION
      *                 FOR GLOBALIZATION.  CONVERT FROM LOWER CASE TO
      *                 UPPER CASE.
      * ----------------------------------------------------------------
      * 03/28/97  BY:   Al Faelschle
      *           DESC: Removed moves to ws-paragraph in abend routines.
      * ----------------------------------------------------------------
      * 02/02/97  BY:   Al Faelschle
      *                 DESC: Removed temporary comments now that the
      *                 copybook has been updated.
      * ----------------------------------------------------------------
      * 11/15/96  BY:   Al Faelschle
      *                 DESC: CONVERTED TO UNIX FOR REHOST PROJECT
      * ----------------------------------------------------------------
      * 08/29/96  BY:   Martin McNabb
      *           DESC: Rehost
      * ----------------------------------------------------------------
      * 11/28/95  BY:   PATTY BECOTTE
      *           DESC: CHANGED TO CHECK 'NAGSTYP' FOR 'N/A'. IF SO, DO
      *                 NOT PRINT, ELSE MOVE VALUE IN CNTL-NAGS-TYP TO
      *                 HEADING.
      * ----------------------------------------------------------------
      * 01/26/95  BY:   PATTY BECOTTE
      *           DESC: CHANGED PROGRAM TO CHECK IF EFFECTIVE DATE
      *                 IS WITHIN 6 MONTHS OF CURRENT DATE.  IF NOT,
      *                 ABEND.
      * ----------------------------------------------------------------
      * 11/15/93  BY:   PENNY GENOVESE
      *           DESC: PROGRAM CREATED FROM MPTZ001.
      *                 TRANS FILE INCREASED FROM 51 TO 100 BYTES.
      *                 (OLD VERSION STILL REQUIRED FOR OEM'S THAT HAVE
      *                 NOT BEEN CONVERTED TO NEW REC FORMAT YET.)
      * ----------------------------------------------------------------
      * 04/01/93  BY:   PENNY GENOVESE
      *           DESC: CHG'D STORAGE OF REPORT INFO TO STORAGE OF RPT
      *                 LINES W/I Oracle TABLE. ADDED CNTL-NAGS-TYP TO
      *                 CNTL-PARM COPYBOOK AND MOVE OF IT'S VALUE TO
      *                 THE HEADING (IF NAGS RUN).
      *****************************************************************

